# Maintainer keys allowed to sign sod release tags.
#
# This file is the trust root for the `verify-tag` gate in .github/workflows/release.yml:
# a release can only be cut from an annotated tag signed by one of these keys. GitHub has
# no native way to require signed *tags* (the `required_signatures` ruleset rule only ever
# checks commits on branches), so this file plus that job is the enforcement point.
#
# Format: <principal> namespaces="git" <keytype> <key>
# The principal must match the tagger's email exactly. `namespaces="git"` scopes the key to
# git signatures, so a key here cannot be used to verify signatures from other namespaces.
#
# Adding or removing a line is a change to who may ship sod — it goes through the same
# reviewed PR as any other change to main.

